###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - The errors are on vibrational free energies integrated from MD power spectra, encoded as energy MAEs in meV/atom; they reflect sampling of the potential energy surface rather than single-point energy errors.
# - The OCP models (EquiformerV2, eSCN, SchNet, PaiNN) are the OC20 S2EF checkpoints of the fairchem calculator; eSCN is a new registry method. The timing is for a whole simulation of one molecule, so no per-atom time is derived (the trajectory length is not restated in Table 1).
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/bechtel2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

